      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Coverage, thresholds and source",
      "description": "Original synthetic mask by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors (MIT). No external images. Pixel-cell area coverage is a software validity model, not physical camera calibration or proof of full cubic/Lanczos interpolation support. Resize 256x192 to 128x96: thresholds one (full area), one-half (inclusive) and zero (any positive area) show different binary masks for holes, alternating columns and a one-pixel invalid line. Empty footprints are never accepted. The target supplies size and has the verified resize frame. Inspect Coverage and the diagnostic heatmap; measurement blocks count each accepted selection on the target grid. This graph performs no equipment I/O.",
      "parameters": {},
      "position": [
        0,
        -350
